        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Amer, William Shakespeare\n- Works: The Tempest, Arrow in the Air\n- Places: Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire\n- Topics: acting careers, stage and screen roles\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote The Tempest, and many critics believe he wrote the play in 1610–11 as the last play he wrote alone.\n- Nicholas Amer was born Thomas Harold Amer on 29 September 1923 in Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire.\n- Nicholas Amer is an English stage, film, and television actor known for performing in William Shakespeare's plays.\n- Nicholas Amer made his professional debut in 1948 by playing Ferdinand in The Tempest.\n- Arrow in the Air starred Nicholas Amer.",
